Reads an OpenHarmony HTTP response's body from net_http's data callback.
Since OpenHarmony 7.0, net_http copies the body it hands the response
callback with strdup, which stops at the body's first NUL byte, but it still
reports the body's full length. A binary response, such as a PMTiles header
or a PNG tile, then read past the end of the copy. The data callback passes
each chunk with its length on every release since API 20.
(https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-native-ffi/issues/1692)
Upstream: https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-native/pull/4932

